IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `priv51-nouns`
IMPORT `priv51-cross-references`

-- Row il-51. The sound citations point at what their citing words say, the rounding arithmetic is what the texts say it is, and the recorded facts about the defects and the controls are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their twenty failing assertions are in priv51-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in priv51-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound citations`

-- The seven controls point at what they say.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: First Schedule item 4(א) to the definition of ראש הרשות`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 12(ג) to s 12(א) and (ב)`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: 1986 regulation 7(ג) to section 23ג`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: 1981 inspection regulation 8 to regulation 5`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: 2023 regulation 7 to regulation 2`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: 2001 regulation 3 to regulation 1`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: 2004 schedule column A to section 17ד`)

§ `Tests of the rounding of an amount in agorot`

-- Nearest multiple of 1000 agorot (ten shekels): a remainder under 500 rounds down, 500 or more rounds up.
#ASSERT `an amount in agorot rounded to the nearest ten shekels` (205) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `an amount in agorot rounded to the nearest ten shekels` (409) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `an amount in agorot rounded to the nearest ten shekels` (819) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `an amount in agorot rounded to the nearest ten shekels` (5118) EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `an amount in agorot rounded to the nearest ten shekels` (10236) EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `an amount in agorot rounded to the nearest ten shekels` (5000) EQUALS 5000

§ `Tests of the per-person rates`

-- The rate of 50 shekels, as the consolidation prints it (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY), is already a multiple of ten; 2 and 4 are not.
#ASSERT `the rate the Law prints is what rounding it to the nearest ten shekels gives` (`rate: 50 shekels, section 23כו(ג)(1)`)
#ASSERT (NOT `the rate the Law prints is what rounding it to the nearest ten shekels gives` (`rate: 2 shekels, section 23כו(ד)(1)`))
#ASSERT (NOT `the rate the Law prints is what rounding it to the nearest ten shekels gives` (`rate: 4 shekels, section 23כו(ה)(1)`))
-- The notice's figures as the page image prints them (51.18, 2.05 and 4.09 shekels), none a multiple of ten shekels.
#ASSERT (`rate: 50 shekels, section 23כו(ג)(1)`)'s `the notice of 7 October 2026 prints, in agorot` EQUALS 5118
#ASSERT (`rate: 2 shekels, section 23כו(ד)(1)`)'s `the notice of 7 October 2026 prints, in agorot` EQUALS 205
#ASSERT (`rate: 4 shekels, section 23כו(ה)(1)`)'s `the notice of 7 October 2026 prints, in agorot` EQUALS 409
#ASSERT (NOT `the rate the notice prints is what rounding it to the nearest ten shekels gives` (`rate: 50 shekels, section 23כו(ג)(1)`))
-- The notice's reading (reading B): the sanction is the rate times the number of persons, rounded after the multiplication.
-- 100 persons at 51.18 shekels is 5,118 shekels, which rounds to 5,120; 7 persons at 2.05 shekels is 14.35 shekels, which rounds to 10.
#ASSERT `the sanction in agorot, rounded after the multiplication` (`rate: 50 shekels, section 23כו(ג)(1)`) (100) EQUALS 512000
#ASSERT `the sanction in agorot, rounded after the multiplication` (`rate: 2 shekels, section 23כו(ד)(1)`) (7) EQUALS 1000

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- No citation here has both limbs read from the official instruments alone: each has a limb that is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY, either the whole limb or that no later instrument touched the words.
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: First Schedule item 4(א) to section 7`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: Third Schedule definition paragraph (3) to the person called בעל מאגר`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: 1986 regulation 1 to section 7`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: 1986 regulation 1 to section 12`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: 1981 inspection regulations 2(א), 5(א) and 7(ב) to the office called הרשם`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: 2023 regulation 7 to section 7`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: 2001 regulations 2 and 3 to the person called בעל מאגר`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: 2004 schedule column A to section 31א(א)(1) to (7)`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: 2004 schedule column A to section 17א(א) and (ב)`))
-- Limb (b) of the three citations in regulations is the consolidation only: no official page of those regulations was read.
#ASSERT (`reference: 1986 regulation 1 to section 7`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: 1986 regulation 1 to section 12`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: 1981 inspection regulations 2(א), 5(א) and 7(ב) to the office called הרשם`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: 2001 regulations 2 and 3 to the person called בעל מאגר`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
-- Limb (b) of P1, P2, P5 and P8 is read from a page image, with the caveat.
#ASSERT (`reference: First Schedule item 4(א) to section 7`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: 2023 regulation 7 to section 7`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: 2004 schedule column A to section 31א(א)(1) to (7)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- Controls: every control has at least one limb that is the consolidation only.
#ASSERT (`reference: 1981 inspection regulation 8 to regulation 5`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: 2023 regulation 7 to regulation 2`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`

§ `Tests of what the two descriptions of the defects say`

